{"id": "23064", "revid": "240096", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=23064", "title": "Morrungulo", "text": "Morrungulo is a town in the central Inhambane Region of Mozambique.\nGet in.\nMorrungulo (also known as Nelson's Bay) turnoff is some 7 km North of Massinga on the main EN1 highway. Turn off at marked Resort sign and go 13 km East down to the beach on a good dirt road. Morrungulo is a family run holiday resort on the secluded clean white beaches of the Indian Ocean.\nAccessed by own vehicle. 4x4 not required.\nDo.\nChill out, swim, fish, scuba dive, bar, restaurant\nEat.\nNew Bar and Restaurant serve good simple meals with Fish dishes straight from the sea.\nDrink.\nClean fresh tap water for drinking on site from own spring/wells.\nSleep.\nChalets, Cassita's and camping on the edge of the beach.\nAll abloutions in Ponta Morrungulo section have gas geysers and power points are available on a daily connection basis from resort power/generators.\nAccommodation covers camping through to self catering chalets on the beach front. Resort has its own clean and safe fresh water supply from a natural spring.\nResort has a Scuba Dive and Fishing Tour operator on site.\nLatitude: 23\u00b014'00.80\"S\nLongitude: 35\u00b029'31.00\"E\nCope.\nNo Quad Bikes allowed in Camp.\nBoat launch requires purchase of Mozambique Port Authority BOAT LICENCES."}
